From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add license-files for vendored boost and yaml-cpp

py-bindings/pyproject.toml sets `license = "BSD-3-Clause"` but declares
no `license-files`, and OMPL's own root LICENSE lives one directory up
from this build's project root (scikit-build-core's `source-dir = ".."`
only governs the CMake configure, not PEP 639 license-file resolution,
which is relative to this pyproject.toml). Confirmed against the real
published wheel (ompl-2.0.1-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux2014_x86_64.whl):
its dist-info ships no licenses/ directory at all, despite statically
linking yaml-cpp (MIT) into libompl.so and vendoring
libboost_serialization (BSL-1.0) alongside the extension via auditwheel.
The build stages copies of all three license texts into this directory
before the build; declaring `license-files` here is what makes
scikit-build-core carry them into `dist-info/licenses/`.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against ompl/ompl]
---
diff --git a/py-bindings/pyproject.toml b/py-bindings/pyproject.toml
index 99c38ad2..f33b4a47 100644
--- a/py-bindings/pyproject.toml
+++ b/py-bindings/pyproject.toml
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@ name = "ompl"
 description = "The Open Motion Planning Library"
 readme = "README.md"
 license = "BSD-3-Clause"
+license-files = ["LICENSE", "LICENSE.boost", "LICENSE.yaml-cpp"]
 dynamic = ["version"]
 requires-python = ">=3.9"
 classifiers = [

